================================================================================
1. OVERVIEW
================================================================================

Rhythm Tap is a single-button rhythm/timing game inspired by games like 
Guitar Hero. Notes continuously scroll down a vertical track, and the 
player must press the button at the exact moment each note reaches the 
"hit zone" near the bottom of the screen. Unlike Stop The Bar (which 
handles ONE moving element per round), Rhythm Tap manages MULTIPLE 
simultaneous notes on screen, each moving independently, testing the 
player's ability to maintain a continuous rhythm rather than react to a 
single isolated event.

Scoring is tiered by accuracy (PERFECT / GOOD / MISS), and the game 
tracks combo streaks that drive progressive difficulty - notes fall 
faster and spawn more frequently as the player's combo grows.

GAME GENRE     : Rhythm / Pattern Timing
CONTROL SCHEME : Single Button (Tap in sync with falling notes)
DIFFICULTY     : Progressive (speed increases & spawn interval decreases 
                 every 8 combo points)
DISPLAY        : 128x64 OLED (SH1106 driver, SPI interface)
MICROCONTROLLER: Arduino Nano

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
HOW TO PLAY
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Power on the device - Start Screen appears showing "RHYTHM TAP"
2. Press the button to begin the game
3. Notes (horizontal bars) continuously spawn at the top of a vertical 
   track and scroll downward
4. A highlighted "hit zone" box sits near the bottom of the track
5. Tap the button exactly when a note overlaps the hit zone:
   - Very close to center = "PERFECT!" (+10 points)
   - Slightly off = "GOOD" (+5 points)
   - Too far off, or no note nearby = "MISS" / "EARLY!" (counts as a miss)
6. Consecutive successful hits build a COMBO streak
7. Every 8 combo points, difficulty increases:
   - Notes fall faster
   - Notes spawn more frequently (up to a minimum interval of 500ms)
8. Missing a note (letting it pass the hit zone) or mistiming a tap both 
   count toward your miss total
9. The game ends after 5 total misses
10. Press the button again on the Game Over screen to return to the 
    start screen and play again

