9. TROUBLESHOOTING
================================================================================

ISSUE: Taps don't register any points even when timed well
FIX: Verify closestDist thresholds (3 for PERFECT, 8 for GOOD) are 
     appropriate for your noteSpeed and frame delay(20) combination. If 
     notes move quickly between frames, the effective "window" of pixel 
     positions that map to a good hit may be narrower than expected - 
     consider increasing thresholds slightly or reducing noteSpeed.

ISSUE: Multiple notes overlap visually and become hard to distinguish
FIX: This can happen if spawnInterval becomes very short (due to high 
     combo/difficulty) while noteSpeed hasn't increased proportionally. 
     Consider tuning the balance between noteSpeed increases and 
     spawnInterval decreases in the difficulty progression logic within 
     handleTap().

ISSUE: "EARLY!" feedback appears even when a note seems visually close
FIX: This occurs when NO note is currently active (closestIndex == -1) 
     - check if your note might have already been removed (either 
     successfully hit moments earlier, or missed/expired) right before 
     your tap registered. This is more likely to happen near spawn 
     boundaries or immediately after a note is cleared.

ISSUE: Game becomes unplayable at high levels (notes too fast)
FIX: The noteSpeed += 0.3 increment per 8-combo milestone can compound 
     quickly during long combo streaks. Consider adding a maximum speed 
     cap (e.g., "if (noteSpeed < 4.0) noteSpeed += 0.3;") to prevent 
     speeds from becoming unreasonably fast during extended skilled play.

ISSUE: bestScore or maxCombo not updating as expected
FIX: bestScore only updates in updateGame() when the game-over condition 
     triggers (misses >= maxMisses). If you exit/restart via other means, 
     ensure this check still executes. maxCombo updates within 
     handleTap() only on successful hits - verify combo is incrementing 
     correctly for both PERFECT and GOOD tiers.

